    "lawCode": "Add §605-g, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5254\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nproviding accidental disability retirement for deputy sheriffs in Nassau\ncounty\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide the option for an accidental disability retirement benefit of\n75% of the final average salary for deputy sheriffs employed by Nassau\nCounty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new Section 605-g to the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law. This new section provides 3/4 accidental disability bene-\nfits to Nassau County deputy sheriffs who were hired on or after July\n27, 1976, and are injured in the line of duty.\n\nSection 2 provides that the cost of implementing this change to the\nRetirement and Social Security Law shall be borne by Nassau County.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn New York, the common accidental disability retirement for members of\nlaw enforcement is an accidental disability retirement equaling a\npercentage of the injured officer's final average salary. As Police\nstatus law enforcement officers, the Nassau County Deputy Sheriffs\nshould be afforded the same accidental disability retirement benefit as\ntheir law enforcement brethren. This bill will treat the Nassau County\nDeputy Sheriffs similarly to other New York law enforcement officers by\nproviding deputy sheriffs who are injured on the job with an accidental\ndisability retirement equaling 3/4 of the injured deputy sheriffs final\naverage salary.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: S.9368 - Referred to Civil Service and Pensions/A.10422 -\nPassed the Assembly\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
